{# ==========================================================
   Custom apidoc package template for bridge
   - Displays public interface (from __init__.py)
   - Then lists subpackages and submodules as tables
   ========================================================== #}

{%- macro automodule(modname, options) -%}
.. automodule:: {{ modname }}
{%- for option in options %}
   :{{ option }}:
{%- endfor %}
{%- endmacro %}


{# ---------- PACKAGE HEADING ---------- #}
{%- if is_namespace %}
{{- [pkgname, "namespace"] | join(" ") | e | heading }}
.. py:module:: {{ pkgname }}
{% else %}
{{- [pkgname, "package"] | join(" ") | e | heading }}
{% endif %}


{# ---------- PUBLIC INTERFACE ---------- #}
Public Interface
----------------
This section documents user-facing interface of the ``{{ pkgname }}`` package (as defined in its ``__init__.py`` file).

.. automodapi:: {{ pkgname }}
   :no-inheritance-diagram:
   :no-main-docstr:
   :include-all-objects:
   :no-heading:
   :noindex:


.. automodule:: {{ pkgname }}
   :members:
   :show-inheritance:



{# ---------- SUBPACKAGES ---------- #}
{%- if subpackages %}
Subpackages
-----------

.. autosummary::
   :toctree: .
   :nosignatures:

   {% for subpackage in subpackages | sort %}
   {{ subpackage | replace(pkgname ~ '.', '') }}
   {% endfor %}
{% endif %}


{# ---------- SUBMODULES ---------- #}
{%- if submodules %}
Submodules
----------

.. autosummary::
   :toctree: .
   :nosignatures:

   {% for submodule in submodules | sort %}
   {{ submodule | replace(pkgname ~ '.', '') }}
   {% endfor %}
{% endif %}


{# ---------- SUBPACKES & SUBMODULES DEPENDENCIES ---------- #}
{%- if subpackages or submodules %}
Dependencies diagram
--------------------

Each architecture diagram below visualizes the internal dependency structure of the ``{{ pkgname }}`` package.
It shows how modules and subpackages within the package depend on each other, based on direct Python imports.

- Packages are shown as purple rectangles
- Modules are shown as pink rectangles
- Arrows (A → B) indicate that A directly imports B

Each subpackage’s diagram focuses only on its own internal structure,
it does not include imports to or from higher-level packages
(those appear in the parent package’s diagram).

.. image:: ../_architecture_generated/{{ pkgname }}.dependencies.svg
   :alt: bridge package dependencies
   :width: 80%
   :align: center

{% endif %}